1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:02,270
From rice farmers
to bullet trains.

2
00:00:02,310 --> 00:00:04,453
This is Japan,
in 60 seconds.

3
00:00:04,493 --> 00:00:07,233
Over 2,000 years ago,
rice farming arrives,

4
00:00:07,273 --> 00:00:10,185
and villages grow
into small kingdoms.

5
00:00:10,225 --> 00:00:13,045
In 710, the court
settles at Nara.

6
00:00:13,085 --> 00:00:15,843
Buddhism spreads,
and great temples rise.

7
00:00:15,883 --> 00:00:18,363
From 1185,
samurai take power,

8
00:00:18,403 --> 00:00:21,103
and the emperor
reigns in name only.

9
00:00:21,143 --> 00:00:24,883
In 1603, the Tokugawa
clan takes over.

10
00:00:24,923 --> 00:00:28,140
Peace follows, and Japan
closes to most of the world.

11
00:00:28,180 --> 00:00:31,660
In 1853, American
warships arrive.

12
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:33,660
Within 15 years,
the shogun falls,

13
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:36,086
and Japan modernises fast.

14
00:00:36,126 --> 00:00:38,726
Growth turns to
empire, and war.

15
00:00:38,766 --> 00:00:43,350
In 1945, atomic bombs destroy
Hiroshima and Nagasaki.

16
00:00:43,390 --> 00:00:46,290
Japan rebuilds. In 1964,

17
00:00:46,330 --> 00:00:49,943
the bullet train opens,
and Tokyo hosts the Olympics.

18
00:00:49,983 --> 00:00:53,023
Today, over 120
million people live

19
00:00:53,063 --> 00:00:55,889
where ancient temples
meet neon cities.

20
00:00:55,929 --> 00:00:59,710
Which country should
we print next?

